<article class="env-corollary" id="060A">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/060A">Corollary <span data-tag="060A">8.5.4.29</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}'$ be the full subcategory of $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}$ spanned by the (small) idempotent-complete $\infty $-categories. Then $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}'$ is closed under small limits in $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      By virtue of Proposition <a data-tag="03UL" href="/tag/03UL">7.6.6.15</a> (with Remark <a data-tag="03UM" href="/tag/03UM">7.6.6.16</a> and Exercise <a data-tag="03J4" href="/tag/03J4">7.6.6.17</a>), it will suffice to show that $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}'$ is closed under pullbacks and small products. The case of pullbacks follows from Corollary <a data-tag="0607" href="/tag/0607">8.5.4.27</a> (see Corollary <a data-tag="03GF" href="/tag/03GF">7.6.3.9</a>), and the case of products follows from Remark <a data-tag="0604" href="/tag/0604">8.5.4.9</a> (see Example <a data-tag="03EP" href="/tag/03EP">7.6.1.20</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
